    "liturgicalCelebration": "Easter Triduum is celebrated in the Holy Week season with white vestments unless rubrics direct otherwise. Liturgy of the Hours during Triduum uses special antiphons and psalms. No other celebrations may take precedence over Triduum liturgies. Easter fire, baptism, and first Eucharist crown the Vigil as Triduum climax. Proper collects and prefaces belong to Easter Triduum — worth reading aloud at home before Mass. Because the date moves, musicians and sacristans should confirm the Ordo before printing worship aids. Arrive early enough to notice the color, the Gloria (or its absence), and the preface — those cues preach before the sermon starts.",
